[h2 [id}abstract{id]}Abstract{h2]
[p}XML namespaces provide a simple method for qualifying element and attribute names used in Extensible Markup Language documents by associating them with namespaces identified by URI references.{p]
[h2 [id}status{id]}Status of this Document{h2]
[p}[em} This section describes the status of this document at the time of its publication. Other documents may supersede this document. A list of current W3C publications and the latest revision of this technical report can be found in the [a [href}https://www.w3.org/TR/{href]}W3C technical reports index{a] at http://www.w3.org/TR/. {em]{p]
[p} This document is a product of the [a [href}https://www.w3.org/XML/Core/{href]}XML Core Working Group{a] as part of the [a [href}https://www.w3.org/XML/Activity.html{href]}W3C XML Activity{a]. The English version of this specification is the only normative version. However, for translations of this document, see [a [href}https://www.w3.org/2003/03/Translations/byTechnology?technology=xml-names{href]} http://www.w3.org/2003/03/Translations/byTechnology?technology=xml-names {a]. {p]
[p} Known implementations are documented in the [a [href}https://www.w3.org/XML/2002/12/xml-names11-implementation.html{href]} Namespaces 1.1 implementation report{a] (all known Namespaces 1.1 implementations also support Namespaces 1.0) . A test suite is also available via the [a [href}https://www.w3.org/XML/Test/{href]}XML Test Suite{a] page. {p]
[p} This third edition incorporates all known errata as of the publication date. It supersedes the previous [a [href}https://www.w3.org/TR/2006/REC-xml-names-20060816/{href]} edition of 16 August 2006{a].{p]
[p}This edition has been widely reviewed. Only minor editorial changes have been made since the 6 August 2009 Proposed Edited Recommendation.{p]
[p} Please report errors in this document to [a [href}mailto:xml-names-editor@w3.org{href]}xml-names-editor@w3.org{a]; public [a [href}http://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/xml-names-editor/{href]}archives{a] are available. The errata list for this document is available at [a [href}https://www.w3.org/XML/2009/xml-names-errata{href]} http://www.w3.org/XML/2009/xml-names-errata {a]. {p]
[p}This document has been reviewed by W3C Members, by software developers, and by other W3C groups and interested parties, and is endorsed by the Director as a W3C Recommendation. It is a stable document and may be used as reference material or cited from another document. W3C's role in making the Recommendation is to draw attention to the specification and to promote its widespread deployment. This enhances the functionality and interoperability of the Web. {p]
