[h2 [id}Philosophy{id]}C The Internal Structure of XML Namespaces (Non-Normative){h2]
[p} This appendix has been deleted. {p]
[h2 [id}changes{id]}D Changes since version 1.0 (Non-Normative){h2]
[p} This version incorporates the errata as of 20 July 2009 [a [href}#errata10{href]}\[1.0 Errata\]{a][a [href}#errata10.2{href]}\[1.0 2e Errata\]{a]. {p]
[p} There are several editorial changes, including a number of terminology changes and additions intended to produce greater consistency. The non-normative appendix "The Internal Structure of XML Namespaces" has been removed. The BNF has been adjusted to interconnect properly with all editions of XML 1.0, including the fifth edition. {p]
[h2 [id}sec-xml-and-sgml{id]}E Acknowledgements (Non-Normative){h2]
[p}This work reflects input from a very large number of people, including especially the participants in the World Wide Web Consortium XML Working Group and Special Interest Group and the participants in the W3C Metadata Activity. The contributions of Charles Frankston of Microsoft were particularly valuable.{p]
[h2 [id}orphans{id]}F Orphaned Productions (Non-Normative){h2]
[p}The following two productions are modified versions of ones which were present in the first two editions of this specification. They are no longer used, but are retained here to satisfy cross-references to undated versions of this specification.{p]
[p}Because the [code}Letter{code] production of XML 1.0, originally used in the definition of [code}NCNameStartChar{code], is no longer the correct basis for defining names since XML 1.0 Fifth Edition, the [code}NCNameStartChar{code] production has been modified to give the correct results against any edition of XML, by defining [code}NCNameStartChar{code] in terms of [a [href}#NT-NCName{href]}NCName{a].{p]
[table}
[tr}
[td [id}NT-NCNameChar{id]}\[5\]   {td]
[td}[code}NCNameChar{code]{td]
[td}   ::=   {td]
[td}[code}[a [href}https://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml/#NT-NameChar{href]}NameChar{a] - ':' [em}/* An XML [a [href}https://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml/#NT-NameChar{href]}NameChar{a], minus the ":" */{em]{code]{td]{tr]
[tr}
[td [id}NT-NCNameStartChar{id]}\[6\]   {td]
[td}[code}NCNameStartChar{code]{td]
[td}   ::=   {td]
[td}[code}[a [href}#NT-NCName{href]}NCName{a] - ( [a [href}https://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml/#NT-Char{href]}Char{a][a [href}https://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml/#NT-Char{href]}Char{a][a [href}https://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml/#NT-Char{href]}Char{a]* ) [em}/* The first letter of an [a [href}#NT-NCName{href]}NCName{a] */{em]{code]{td]{tr]{table]
[p}[strong}Note:{strong]{p]
[p}Production [a [href}#NT-NCNameStartChar{href]}NC-NCNameStartChar{a] takes advantage of the fact that a single-character NCName is necessarily an NCNameStartChar, and works by subtracting from the set of NCNames of all lengths the set of all strings of two or more characters, leaving only the NCNames which are one character long.{p]{article]